From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:47:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: raise the shared notifier's count at each
 render's publish

Metal raises a command buffer notifier's Work count as each of its
renders is published (2, 4, 6, ... in the 2026-10-27 HV capture), not
to the command buffer's total up front. Do the same: the owner writes
the header with count 2, each later render of the submission writes the
raised count with its driver stamps. The count then never runs ahead of
what was published, so a submission cut short (a rejected or abandoned
render) leaves no notifier waiting for Works that never come, and the
under-count report and the remaining-render count go away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 267a76653a17f7c58292d90ecb6e5ed9c6da8fd1)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm_pump.rs       | 13 ++---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs        |  2 -
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime_render.rs | 60 ++++++++++++---------
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime_retire.rs | 24 ---------
 4 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

